{"record": "turn", "turn": 4, "seconds": 5.969, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["thinking", "tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 10936, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 947, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_01LvnAo2TLNAS8wY7e74QCM7", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"answer": "No. The two analyses use different likelihood-ratio thresholds and profile different nuisance parameters. dSph gamma-ray limits: the paper sets a one-sided 95% upper limit where 2ΔlnL (ΔTS) = 2.71, and profiles over the per-dwarf J-factor normalization (J = sJ0, Gaussian prior from the stellar-kinematic uncertainty, log10 s in [-3,3]). AMS-02 antiproton limits: the upper limit is the upper endpoint of the ΔQ = Δ(-2lnL) ≤ 3.84 region. The paper says this is the nominal 95% threshold for one parameter of interest, and that it differs from the one-sided 2.71 prescription. It profiles over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, with a Gaussian penalty in log10 L centred at 4.96 kpc with σ = 0.197, over 1 ≤ L/kpc ≤ 12.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261120T075320Z_dev-02_staged_7d48", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "No. The two analyses use different likelihood-ratio thresholds and profile different nuisance parameters. dSph gamma-ray limits: the paper sets a one-sided 95% upper limit where 2ΔlnL (ΔTS) = 2.71, and profiles over the per-dwarf J-factor normalization (J = sJ0, Gaussian prior from the stellar-kinematic uncertainty, log10 s in [-3,3]). AMS-02 antiproton limits: the upper limit is the upper endpoint of the ΔQ = Δ(-2lnL) ≤ 3.84 region. The paper says this is the nominal 95% threshold for one parameter of interest, and that it differs from the one-sided 2.71 prescription. It profiles over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, with a Gaussian penalty in log10 L centred at 4.96 kpc with σ = 0.197, over 1 ≤ L/kpc ≤ 12.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}]}, "turns": 4, "seconds": 11.091, "tool_calls": 4, "tool_result_chars": 19377, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1267, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 25367, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-20T07:53:32+00:00"}
